{
  "diagnoses": [
    {
      "preserve": "The motivations are missing updates, missing RTSP support, and other firmware not using the latest stock firmware, which includes improvements.",
      "problem": "“The answer is simple” adds empty framing, while “new cool stuff” substitutes enthusiasm for a description. The uneven list also leaves readers to infer that RTSP is missing and what is not based on current stock firmware.",
      "quote": "The answer is simple: missing updates, RTSP and not based on the latest stock firmware (which features improvements and new cool stuff).",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 1
    },
    {
      "preserve": "Credit the other projects and retain the acknowledgment that this version depended on their work.",
      "problem": "“Effort and work” duplicates the same idea, and “the making of this new version” adds an indirect construction to an otherwise straightforward acknowledgment.",
      "quote": "The effort and work that has been put into the other projects is great and without them the making of this new version wouldn't be possible.",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 2
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The reported encoder fixes, retained app functionality, and option to disable that functionality.",
      "problem": "“Everything works as it should” is an unbounded assurance. The surrounding text supports particular encoder fixes and tests on named platforms, rather than an unrestricted claim about every function.",
      "quote": "Now everything works as it should and the app functionalities are intact (but they can be disabled if you want).",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 7
    },
    {
      "preserve": "Gratitude for donations and cameras supplied for testing, and the intention to reward supporters with first access to testing new functionality.",
      "problem": "The extended gratitude preamble and “I would like to reward them allowing to be the first ones” bury the concrete early-access benefit in a cumbersome chain of clauses. “Really” adds emphasis without explaining the support.",
      "quote": "I'm really thankful to those who supported the project and helped me by donating or sending me new cameras to test on, therefore I would like to reward them allowing to be the first ones to test the new functionalities.",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 13
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The distinction between listed firmware features, features in development, and features that might be added.",
      "problem": "This introductory sentence repeats the “Features” heading and immediately precedes another “NEW FEATURES” label, creating three layers of framing before any feature appears.",
      "quote": "This firmware will add the following features:",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 23
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The web server provides statistics and configuration functionality.",
      "problem": "“User-friendly” asserts an ease-of-use benefit without identifying any supporting interface behavior. The concrete information here is the availability of statistics and configuration.",
      "quote": "WebServer - user-friendly stats and configurations.",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 30
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The listed cameras are currently supported; proposed or unsupported models must remain distinguishable.",
      "problem": "The sentence repeats the immediately preceding “Supported cameras” heading without adding a support condition or helping readers interpret the list.",
      "quote": "Currently this project supports the following cameras:",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 46
    },
    {
      "preserve": "Users must verify that their Xiaomi Yi camera is among the supported models in the preceding section.",
      "problem": "“A correct Xiaomi Yi camera” leaves the verification criterion vague. The preceding model list supplies the specific criterion: supported-model membership.",
      "quote": "Check that you have a correct Xiaomi Yi camera. (see the section above)",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 54
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The expected result is a FAT32 partition on the microSD card that enables the camera to load firmware files for the yi-hack-v4 update; retain the protected identifier.",
      "problem": "The chain “that will allow … to load … to update to” makes the relationship between the partition and firmware update unnecessarily difficult to follow.",
      "quote": "You should now have a FAT32 partition on your microSD card that will allow the camera to load the firmware files to update to",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 78
    },
    {
      "preserve": "Every camera-to-filename mapping, both required partition files for each supported model, and the separate “Not yet supported” remark for Yi Home.",
      "problem": "This remark repeats the camera name and the requirement already expressed by the row and partition columns. The same boilerplate occupies every supported-camera remark, making the table longer without adding model-specific guidance.",
      "quote": "Firmware files required for the Yi Home 17CN / 27US / 47US camera.",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 90
    },
    {
      "preserve": "Access the camera's web interface in a browser, retaining the following default hostname and URL instructions.",
      "problem": "“Access the web interface … as a website” explains the same action twice, and the following sentence after the hostname repeats the browser-access instruction with the actual address.",
      "quote": "Go in the browser and access the web interface of the camera as a website.",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 119
    },
    {
      "preserve": "When multiple cameras are present, each needs a unique hostname; otherwise access is only available by IP address.",
      "problem": "“It is important to” repeats the immediately preceding “IMPORTANT” label and delays the concrete configuration requirement. The stated consequence already explains why the requirement matters.",
      "quote": "It is important to configure each camera with a unique hostname.",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 127
    }
  ],
  "page_id": "TheCrypt0/yi-hack-v4/README.md",
